# @hub-lanes

# ── TICKET STATUS COMMENT LANE (BH-9503, C1 of #8973) ───────────────────────
# Every 5 minutes. --dispatch reads nothing: it starts one detached
# `ticket-status-comment.sh <project>` per fleet project, each on its own lock
# and at a stable offset inside TICKET_STATUS_COMMENT_SPREAD_S
# (bin/lib/project-lanes.sh). A watched GitHub-issues project
# (TICKET_STATUS_COMMENT_PROJECTS, default cromford only) asks the worker
# which tickets' status changed (GET /api/ticket-status-comments/due) and edits
# each ticket's ONE status comment in place, or posts it once.
# Off: flags/lane-off-ticket-status-comment (bin/harness-ctl.sh off
# ticket-status-comment), or TICKET_STATUS_COMMENT_ENABLED=0.
*/5 * * * * /root/harness/bin/hub-lease.sh check && /root/harness/bin/ticket-status-comment.sh --dispatch >> /root/harness/logs/ticket-status-comment-cron.log 2>&1
